    "FR-A800 series"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "FR-A800 series inverters (FR-A820/A840/A842/A846, incl. -GF) using the built-in RS-485 terminals with Pr.549 = 1 (MODBUS RTU); Instruction Manual (Detailed) revision P.",
  "summary": "Mitsubishi Electric's high-performance general-purpose inverter. Its RS-485 terminal block can speak Modbus RTU, exposing system variables (control word, operation mode, frequency command) at 40002-40015, a real-time monitor block from 40201, fault history at 40501, and parameters at 41000 + parameter number (Pr.1000 and up at 44000 + parameter number). This map covers control, status, the main monitors and the communication parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The manual prints Modicon-style register numbers (40002, 41004). Its rule: starting address = register number - 40001, e.g. reading 41004 (Pr.4) sends start address H03EB (1003)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "FR-A800 Instruction Manual (Detailed)",
    "doc_number": "IB(NA)-0600503ENG-P",
    "revision_date": "2026-04",
    "url": "https://dl.mitsubishielectric.com/dl/fa/document/manual/inv/ib0600503eng/ib0600503engp.pdf",
    "pages": "Printed pp. 464-469 (monitor item list with MODBUS RTU column, terminal bit layouts), pp. 714-726 (Modbus RTU specification, frame example p. 719, MODBUS register tables pp. 723-726), pp. 395-396 (Pr.79), parameter list chapter 5.1 (increments)."
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are single 16-bit words. The manual notes that a 32-bit parameter or monitor whose value exceeds HFFFF reads back as HFFFF.",
    "Left out because the increment depends on inverter capacity (0.01 unit up to FR-A820-03160(55K)/FR-A840-01800(55K), 0.1 unit above): output current 40202, output current peak 40211, input power 40213, output power 40214, motor excitation current 40218, cumulative energy 40225, motor output 40234 and the 32-bit cumulative energy halves 40279/40280. Motor load factor 40224 (% of rated current) gives a size-independent current reading.",
    "Left out because sign handling is unclear (footnote *1 says Modbus cannot carry a minus sign, footnote *20 says Pr.1018 enables signed monitors): motor torque 40207, torque 40236, PID deviation 40254, second PID deviation 40294, PID manipulated amounts, remote output values and control circuit temperature 40298. Output frequency 40201 and operation speed 40206 are kept as unsigned: they only become signed when Pr.1018 is set. Vector-control position/pulse monitors (40219-40231, 40271-40275) are also left out.",
    "Output frequency, set frequency and the frequency command use 0.01 Hz by default; with Pr.37 = 1-9998 or Pr.144 = 2-12/102-112 the increment becomes 1 (speed display), and Pr.811 also affects the 40014/40015 display. The 0.01 Hz unit for 40014/40015 comes from the same manual's computer-link set-frequency description (H0000-HFFFF in 0.01 Hz increments).",
    "Fault history registers hold the error code in the low byte (high byte H00); code meanings are in the manual's fault chapter.",
    "Parameters 0-999 sit at 41000 + Pr. number and 1000-1999 at 44000 + Pr. number. Calibration parameters C2-C45 have their own registers (41902-43935) and are not listed.",
    "Parameters with a 9999 (function off) setting, such as the communication check interval, are listed with their normal increment; the manual does not say how the 9999 setting itself is encoded on the wire, so read the parameter back after setting it from the panel.",
    "Pr.7/Pr.8 acceleration/deceleration times are left out: their increment changes with Pr.21."
  ],
